# Files Prettier must not rewrite.
#
# Everything here is *generated*. Formatting a generated file is churn at best:
# the tool that produces it writes it back in its own style on the next run, so
# the file oscillates and `pnpm format:check` fails again for reasons no human
# can act on.
#
# pnpm-lock.yaml is the clearest case - it is pnpm's output, pnpm rewrites it on
# every dependency change, and a Prettier pass over it would be undone by the
# next `pnpm install`. Confirmed empirically: running `prettier --write .` over
# it once rewrote every single-line `resolution: {integrity: ...}`/`engines: {...}`
# flow mapping onto several lines - a ~1000-line diff on a file no human edits,
# which would make every future dependency-touching PR noisy and conflict-prone.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Timestamped benchmark and capability-check output. These are measurement
# records written by scripts/run-*-benchmark.mjs and
# scripts/run-*-capability-check.mjs as committed proof of a real run;
# reformatting them edits recorded evidence.
benchmarks/results/

# Build output.
**/dist/
**/coverage/

# Rust build artifacts and generated wasm bindings.
rust/target/
packages/*/wasm/
